==Problem 13==

Two congruent squares, <imath>ABCD</imath> and <imath>PQRS</imath>, have side length <imath>15</imath>. They overlap to form the <imath>15</imath> by <imath>25</imath> rectangle <imath>AQRD</imath> shown. What percent of the area of rectangle <imath>AQRD</imath> is shaded? 
<asy>
filldraw((0,0)--(25,0)--(25,15)--(0,15)--cycle,white,black);
label("D",(0,0),S);
label("R",(25,0),S);
label("Q",(25,15),N);
label("A",(0,15),N);
filldraw((10,0)--(15,0)--(15,15)--(10,15)--cycle,mediumgrey,black);
label("S",(10,0),S);
label("C",(15,0),S);
label("B",(15,15),N);
label("P",(10,15),N);</asy>

<imath> \textbf{(A)}\ 15\qquad\textbf{(B)}\ 18\qquad\textbf{(C)}\ 20\qquad\textbf{(D)}\ 24\qquad\textbf{(E)}\ 25 </imath>

